course: dictionary
lesson: 6132
title: Migrate: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Swallows migrate to warm Africa every autumn and come back in spring.» The clues are every autumn, come back in spring, and warm Africa. So migrate means to make a long journey to a warmer place at a certain time of year.
explain: The same word works for people. «Many families today are migrants» means people who have moved to live in another country, usually to find work or a better life. The context tells you which meaning is meant: seasons and animals for birds, countries and work for families.
explain: Computers use the word too: to migrate data means to move information to a new system. Always ask what is moving and why. Then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Migrate is a verb. Migration is the noun, as in «bird migration», and migratory is the adjective, as in «migratory birds».
fact: «Migrate» means to move from one area to another at certain seasons, often very far, to find food, warmth or a place to breed.
fact: «Migrate» can also mean to move to live in another country or area, usually to find work or a better life.
fact: Some animals migrate, including whales, salmon, wildebeest and some butterflies.
fact: In computing, «migrate» means to move data or programs to a new system.
exercise: «Swallows migrate to warm Africa every autumn and come back in spring.» What does migrate mean here? | To sleep in a nest through the winter | *To make a long journey to a warmer place at a certain time of year | To fly around the garden all day | To sing loudly in the spring
exercise: «Many families today are migrants.» What does migrants mean? | Children who play outside | *People who have moved to live in another country | Animals that fly south for winter | Computers with new programs
exercise: Which word is the noun for the action of migrating? | Migrating | Migratory | Migrated | *Migration
test: Which animal in the lesson swims back up rivers? | Swallow | *Salmon | Goose | Monarch butterfly
test: What does it mean to migrate data? | *To move it to a new system | To delete it forever | To print it out | To make it louder
exam: Geese ___ south every winter to find warmth and food. Which word fits best? | Sleep | Hide | Sing | *Migrate
